	"_comment": "THE pattern content-type taxonomy (spec 2026-10-17-pattern-catalog-browse \u00a73.2): one declaration of what a pattern is, in page order, read by Pattern_Taxonomy (the one classifier and normalizer), by bin/generate-taxonomy.php (which validates it and writes taxonomy-i18n.php), by bin/bundled-patterns-check.php (BP-keyword, BP-type, BP-title, BP-name) and by the theme's pattern gates. Untranslated data only: labels are translated through the generated taxonomy-i18n.php, and a feature that is a catalog unit carries its unit id, never a label (\u00a713 F11). Edit this file, then run php bin/generate-taxonomy.php; --check fails a stale i18n file or any TAXONOMY# rule. Families (spec 2026-10-17-pattern-families \u00a73.3): layout_values (the closed set of Layout option ids, labeled), layout_ops (per block, the attribute paths a derived member may change and the values each admits: a list of enum values, or preset:<kind> for a var:preset reference; null always clears), families (one card each: a base, its derived members as ops, its header and footer siblings) and renamed (a retired pattern's family and layout, or the pattern it folded into). FAMILY# rules live in Pattern_Taxonomy::problems().",
